        <p class="profile-detail-region">Life · Central &amp; East Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Kublai Khan</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1215 CE – 1294 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">23 September 1215; the fourth son of Tolui, and his second by his chief wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sorghaghtani-beki">Sorghaghtani Beki</a>; a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a>, of the House of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borjigin">Borjigin</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">18 February 1294, aged 78, after a long decline in health with gout and diabetes; taken for burial to the burial place of the Khans in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Viceroy over northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> (from 1251); <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-khan">Great Khan</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">Khagan</a>) of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> (1260–1294); founder and first emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a> (1271–1294), temple name Shizu, regnal name Setsen Khan</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a>; completing the conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song dynasty</a>; the capitals <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dadu">Dadu</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khanbaliq">Khanbaliq</a>, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>) and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shangdu">Shangdu</a> (Xanadu); a unified paper currency; the failed invasions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>; patronage of the Phags pa Lama and of Muslim scientists; receiving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marco-polo">Marco Polo</a></span></div>
        </div>
