    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Kublai's proclamation as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-khan">Great Khan</a> in 1260, against the election of his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ariq-boke">Ariq Böke</a>, led to a civil war lasting until 1264 and marked the beginning of the division of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a>.</li><li>He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> his base, proclaimed the dynastic name Great Yuan in 1271 and destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> by 1279, becoming the first non-Han emperor to rule all of China proper.</li><li>His invasions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> failed or won only nominal submission, and their cost, with the expansion of paper currency, caused <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inflation">inflation</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In August 1260 Kublai created the first unified paper currency, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiaochao">Jiaochao</a>, circulated throughout his domain with no expiration date; he is considered to be the first maker of fiat money.</p></aside>
    </section>

